{"toolCallId":"call_2559e33f57664051b0db105b96e4e0de","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write `not a consumer` when it does not read the change. Write `N/A` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n\nUse this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: producer/helper/policy] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: what owns the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: consumer/status/docs/tests] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: how it observes the behavior] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: update/unchanged/not a consumer] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: grep/test/doc evidence] |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `rg -n '<field|string|helper|literal|error-pattern>' <module-or-files>`.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<changedSymbol>|<changedConstant>|<changedPublicField>' . --glob '*.ts' --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'`.\n- Matrix axes: list every independent input axis and the required rows before implementation.\n- Algorithm invariant: for path/redaction/parser/resolver/security fixes, state the invariant and adversarial cases.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Components/functions] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Jest/pytest/etc.] |\n| Integration | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: API endpoints/flows] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Tools] |\n| Manual | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: User journeys] | Browser |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/Library] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Internal/External] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Green/Yellow/Red] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Impact] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n- **Trigger**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Conditions requiring rollback]\n- **Procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to revert changes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Draw the phase order in the fence, then fill the table with depends-on and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup to Implementation to Verification. Verification blocks close. WEAK: Phases depend on each other. -->\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──────┐\n                      ├──► Phase 2 (Core) ──► Phase 3 (Verify)\nPhase 1.5 (Config) ───┘\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Core, Config |\n| Config | Setup | Core |\n| Core | Setup, Config | Verify |\n| Verify | Core | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n<!-- FILL: Give each phase an estimate and a total. Mark the total as an assumption. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Setup 10 minutes, implementation 30, verification 10. Total 50 minutes. WEAK: A few hours. -->\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| Core Implementation | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 4-8 hours] |\n| Verification | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Low/Med/High] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 1-2 hours] |\n| **Total** | | **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., 6-12 hours]** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger, the steps and the data reversal. Write `No` when no data changes. Delete the whole section when the packet ships no deployable service. GOOD: Trigger: default output changes. Steps: revert one commit, rerun the two commands. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes)\n- [ ] Feature flag configured\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n2. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n3. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n4. [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Yes/No]\n- **Reversal procedure**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Steps or \"N/A\"]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n<!-- FILL: Draw the component order and fill the matrix with produces and blocks. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Script to test to close. WEAK: Components depend on each other. -->\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └──────┬──────┘     └─────────────┘\n                          │\n                    ┌─────▼─────┐\n                    │  Phase 2b │\n                    │  Parallel │\n                    └───────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component A] | None | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | B, C |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component B] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component C] | A | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Output] | D |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component D] | B, C | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Final] | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n<!-- FILL: Name the longest chain and its total. List what can run in parallel. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Implementation to verification, 40 minutes. Docs run in parallel. WEAK: The critical path is the main path. -->\n\n1. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n2. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n3. **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Phase/Task]** - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Duration estimate] - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Sum of durations]\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task A] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task B] can run simultaneously\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task C] and [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Task D] can run after Phase 1\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n<!-- FILL: Name three milestones with a command-checkable success criterion. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: M1: the branch exists. `rg -n quiet` prints it. WEAK: Milestones are tracked. -->\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Setup Complete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All dependencies ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M2 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Core Done] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Main features working] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n| M3 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Release Ready] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: All tests pass] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Date/Phase] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n<!-- FILL: Write one ADR per decision. Name the context, the choice, the consequence and the rejected option. GOOD: ADR-001: a flag, because callers already pass flags. WEAK: We made a decision. -->\n\n### ADR-001: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Decision Title]\n\n**Status**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n\n**Context**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What problem we're solving]\n\n**Decision**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What we decided]\n\n**Consequences**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Positive outcome 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Negative outcome + mitigation]\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Option B]: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Why rejected]\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one output branch, one parser case and one conflict check to a single bash script; prove it with a line count and a byte comparison.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell; the script already sets `set -euo pipefail` |\n| **Framework** | None — a single CLI script |\n| **Storage** | None — the script is stateless |\n| **Testing** | `bash -n` for syntax plus shell assertions with `wc -l`, `diff` and `grep` |\n\n### Overview\nChange one file, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`. Add a `QUIET` global, a `--quiet` case in the existing parser, a conflict check against `--json`, and an early branch in `output_text()` that prints the level line and returns. Prove it by counting lines in both modes and by diffing the quiet line against the default report's level line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] `sed -n '656,719p' recommend-level.sh` shows the parser block this change extends\n- [ ] `recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints 17\n- [ ] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0 before the first edit\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is Met\n- [ ] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0 after the last edit\n- [ ] The quiet run prints 1 line and the default run prints 17\n- [ ] `diff` of the default report against the pre-change baseline prints nothing\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-script output branch.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]` with `case \"$1\"`): turns argv into globals, one case per flag.\n- **`output_text()`**: writes the human report and owns the `Recommended Level:` line.\n- **`output_json()`**: writes the machine document; unchanged by this feature.\n- **`show_help()`**: renders the option list the flag must join.\n\n### Data Flow\nargv reaches the parser, which sets `LOC`, `FILES`, the four risk booleans, `JSON_OUTPUT` and the new `QUIET`. The score helpers turn those into `TOTAL_SCORE`, then `determine_level` sets `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `LEVEL_NAME`. The output dispatch at the end of the script chooses `output_json` when `JSON_OUTPUT` is true, otherwise `output_text`, which prints the level line alone when `QUIET` is true and the full report otherwise.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` | Producer: owns the level line and the whole report | update | `grep -n 'Recommended Level' recommend-level.sh` prints one line |\n| Callers in skill workflows and docs | Consumers of stdout text; none parses the report programmatically | unchanged | `grep -rn 'recommend-level' .skilled/skills --include='*.sh'` returns the script itself only |\n| `--json` consumers | Read the JSON document, which `--quiet` never touches | not a consumer | `--json` output diffed before and after the change |\n| Script tests | No test file covers this script today | not a consumer | `ls runtime/cli/tests | grep -i recommend` prints nothing |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `grep -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` prints one line, so the label has a single producer.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `grep -rn 'recommend-level' .skilled/skills --include='*.sh'` finds no second script that calls it.\n- Matrix axes: output mode (text, quiet, json) × input validity (valid, missing required inputs, unknown option, conflicting mode).\n- Algorithm invariant: not applicable — this change adds no path, parser, redaction or resolver logic.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | Parser acceptance for `--quiet`, the `--json` conflict and the unknown-option path | bash invocations, `$?`, stderr capture |\n| Integration | The text-output branch through `output_text()` | `wc -l` and `diff` against the pre-change baseline |\n| Regression | Default report and JSON document for the reference invocation | `diff` of pre-change and post-change output |\n| Manual | `--help` renders the new option in the same column format | `grep -c -- '--quiet'` on the help output |\n\nThe two assertions that decide the feature are a line count and a byte comparison: `--quiet` must print `1` line, and that line must equal the default report's `Recommended Level:` line byte for byte.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| bash 3.2+ | Internal | Green | The script cannot run; every verification step stops |\n| coreutils (`wc`, `diff`, `grep`) | Internal | Green | Verification assertions cannot be expressed; implementation still possible |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: The default report changes, the level line moves, or the quiet run prints anything other than one line.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single commit that touches `recommend-level.sh`. The flag is additive and the script holds no state, so no data or configuration needs unwinding.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──► Phase 2 (Implementation) ──► Phase 3 (Verification)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Implementation |\n| Implementation | Setup | Verification |\n| Verification | Implementation | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 20 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 15 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **45 minutes (assumption)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes) — no data changes, so none needed\n- [ ] Feature flag configured — not applicable; the new flag is opt-in by invocation\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set — not applicable; no service is deployed\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the commit that modifies `recommend-level.sh`.\n2. Run `bash -n` on the restored file.\n3. Re-run the reference invocation and confirm 17 lines and exit 0.\n4. Notify callers only if the flag had already been announced.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A — the script writes no file and holds no state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture | None | Pre-change report and JSON fixtures | Implementation, Verification |\n| Parser and output branch | Baseline capture | One-line quiet mode | Verification |\n| Verification | Parser and output branch | Line-count and byte-equality evidence | Close |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Capture the pre-change baseline** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Add the parser case, conflict check and output branch** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Run the line-count and byte-equality checks** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: 45 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- Header and help text edits can land alongside the parser case once the wording is fixed.\n- The JSON regression check can run while the text-mode checks run, because neither writes a file.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | `recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints 17 | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Quiet mode works | `... --quiet | wc -l` prints 1 and `diff` of the level lines is empty | Phase 2 |\n| M3 | Nothing else moved | Default report and JSON document diff clean against the baseline, `bash -n` exits 0 | Phase 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Gate the level line inside `output_text` instead of adding a second output function\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: The script has one text renderer, `output_text()`, which writes 17 lines including the level line. Quiet mode needs one of those lines and none of the others.\n\n**Decision**: Add a `QUIET` global set by the parser, then branch inside `output_text()` so it prints the level line and returns before the score, breakdown and phase blocks. Both modes read the same `echo`, so the line has one definition.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- The quiet line cannot drift from the report's level line, because both come from the same statement.\n- The function gains one early branch, and the phase block still computes in quiet mode; that arithmetic is wasted and is accepted so output and computation stay separate concerns.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- A separate `output_quiet()` function: duplicates the label string, so the two copies can drift.\n- Having callers pipe the report through `grep`: costs a second process, hides the script's own answer, and breaks on a label change just the same.\n\n### ADR-002: Reject `--quiet --json` with exit 1 instead of letting one flag win\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: `--json` already emits a single machine document, and `--quiet` emits a single text line. A caller that passes both has asked for two different outputs.\n\n**Decision**: The parser records both booleans, and a check immediately after the parse loop writes an error naming both flags to stderr and exits 1.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- A contradictory invocation fails loudly instead of returning a shape the caller did not ask for.\n- Callers must choose one mode, and the help text states the exclusion so the failure is predictable.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- JSON wins silently: the caller receives a document while believing it asked for a line, so the mistake surfaces far from its cause.\n- Quiet wins: a JSON consumer that adds the flag loses its document without a diagnostic.\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":91,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":92}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_27f4447f888a45519423339018a23a1e","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one output branch, one parser case and one conflict check to a single bash script; prove it with a line count and a byte comparison.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell; the script already sets `set -euo pipefail` |\n| **Framework** | None — a single CLI script |\n| **Storage** | None — the script is stateless |\n| **Testing** | `bash -n` for syntax plus shell assertions with `wc -l`, `diff` and `grep` |\n\n### Overview\nChange one file, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`. Add a `QUIET` global, a `--quiet` case in the existing parser, a conflict check against `--json`, and an early branch in `output_text()` that prints the level line and returns. Prove it by counting lines in both modes and by diffing the quiet line against the default report's level line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] `sed -n '656,719p' recommend-level.sh` shows the parser block this change extends\n- [ ] `recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints 17\n- [ ] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0 before the first edit\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is Met\n- [ ] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0 after the last edit\n- [ ] The quiet run prints 1 line and the default run prints 17\n- [ ] `diff` of the default report against the pre-change baseline prints nothing\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-script output branch.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]` with `case \"$1\"`): turns argv into globals, one case per flag.\n- **`output_text()`**: writes the human report and owns the `Recommended Level:` line.\n- **`output_json()`**: writes the machine document; unchanged by this feature.\n- **`show_help()`**: renders the option list the flag must join.\n\n### Data Flow\nargv reaches the parser, which sets `LOC`, `FILES`, the four risk booleans, `JSON_OUTPUT` and the new `QUIET`. The score helpers turn those into `TOTAL_SCORE`, then `determine_level` sets `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `LEVEL_NAME`. The output dispatch at the end of the script chooses `output_json` when `JSON_OUTPUT` is true, otherwise `output_text`, which prints the level line alone when `QUIET` is true and the full report otherwise.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` | Producer: owns the level line and the whole report | update | `grep -n 'Recommended Level' recommend-level.sh` prints one line |\n| Callers in skill workflows and docs | Consumers of stdout text; none parses the report programmatically | unchanged | `grep -rn 'recommend-level' .skilled/skills --include='*.sh'` returns the script itself only |\n| `--json` consumers | Read the JSON document, which `--quiet` never touches | not a consumer | `--json` output diffed before and after the change |\n| Script tests | No test file covers this script today | not a consumer | `ls runtime/cli/tests | grep -i recommend` prints nothing |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `grep -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` prints one line, so the label has a single producer.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `grep -rn 'recommend-level' .skilled/skills --include='*.sh'` finds no second script that calls it.\n- Matrix axes: output mode (text, quiet, json) × input validity (valid, missing required inputs, unknown option, conflicting mode).\n- Algorithm invariant: not applicable — this change adds no path, parser, redaction or resolver logic.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | Parser acceptance for `--quiet`, the `--json` conflict and the unknown-option path | bash invocations, `$?`, stderr capture |\n| Integration | The text-output branch through `output_text()` | `wc -l` and `diff` against the pre-change baseline |\n| Regression | Default report and JSON document for the reference invocation | `diff` of pre-change and post-change output |\n| Manual | `--help` renders the new option in the same column format | `grep -c -- '--quiet'` on the help output |\n\nThe two assertions that decide the feature are a line count and a byte comparison: `--quiet` must print `1` line, and that line must equal the default report's `Recommended Level:` line byte for byte.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| bash 3.2+ | Internal | Green | The script cannot run; every verification step stops |\n| coreutils (`wc`, `diff`, `grep`) | Internal | Green | Verification assertions cannot be expressed; implementation still possible |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: The default report changes, the level line moves, or the quiet run prints anything other than one line.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single commit that touches `recommend-level.sh`. The flag is additive and the script holds no state, so no data or configuration needs unwinding.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──► Phase 2 (Implementation) ──► Phase 3 (Verification)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Implementation |\n| Implementation | Setup | Verification |\n| Verification | Implementation | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 20 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 15 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **45 minutes (assumption)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes) — no data changes, so none needed\n- [ ] Feature flag configured — not applicable; the new flag is opt-in by invocation\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set — not applicable; no service is deployed\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the commit that modifies `recommend-level.sh`.\n2. Run `bash -n` on the restored file.\n3. Re-run the reference invocation and confirm 17 lines and exit 0.\n4. Notify callers only if the flag had already been announced.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A — the script writes no file and holds no state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture | None | Pre-change report and JSON fixtures | Implementation, Verification |\n| Parser and output branch | Baseline capture | One-line quiet mode | Verification |\n| Verification | Parser and output branch | Line-count and byte-equality evidence | Close |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Capture the pre-change baseline** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Add the parser case, conflict check and output branch** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Run the line-count and byte-equality checks** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: 45 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- Header and help text edits can land alongside the parser case once the wording is fixed.\n- The JSON regression check can run while the text-mode checks run, because neither writes a file.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | `recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints 17 | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Quiet mode works | `... --quiet | wc -l` prints 1 and `diff` of the level lines is empty | Phase 2 |\n| M3 | Nothing else moved | Default report and JSON document diff clean against the baseline, `bash -n` exits 0 | Phase 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Gate the level line inside `output_text` instead of adding a second output function\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: The script has one text renderer, `output_text()`, which writes 17 lines including the level line. Quiet mode needs one of those lines and none of the others.\n\n**Decision**: Add a `QUIET` global set by the parser, then branch inside `output_text()` so it prints the level line and returns before the score, breakdown and phase blocks. Both modes read the same `echo`, so the line has one definition.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- The quiet line cannot drift from the report's level line, because both come from the same statement.\n- The function gains one early branch, and the phase block still computes in quiet mode; that arithmetic is wasted and is accepted so output and computation stay separate concerns.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- A separate `output_quiet()` function: duplicates the label string, so the two copies can drift.\n- Having callers pipe the report through `grep`: costs a second process, hides the script's own answer, and breaks on a label change just the same.\n\n### ADR-002: Reject `--quiet --json` with exit 1 instead of letting one flag win\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: `--json` already emits a single machine document, and `--quiet` emits a single text line. A caller that passes both has asked for two different outputs.\n\n**Decision**: The parser records both booleans, and a check immediately after the parse loop writes an error naming both flags to stderr and exits 1.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- A contradictory invocation fails loudly instead of returning a shape the caller did not ask for.\n- Callers must choose one mode, and the help text states the exclusion so the failure is predictable.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- JSON wins silently: the caller receives a document while believing it asked for a line, so the mistake surfaces far from its cause.\n- Quiet wins: a JSON consumer that adds the flag loses its document without a diagnostic.\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one output branch, one parser case and one conflict check to a single bash script; prove it with a line count and a byte comparison.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell; the script already sets `set -euo pipefail` |\n| **Framework** | None — a single CLI script |\n| **Storage** | None — the script is stateless |\n| **Testing** | `bash -n` for syntax plus shell assertions with `wc -l`, `diff` and `grep` |\n\n### Overview\nChange one file, `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`. Add a `QUIET` global, a `--quiet` case in the existing parser, a conflict check against `--json`, and an early branch in `output_text()` that prints the level line and returns. Prove it by counting lines in both modes and by diffing the quiet line against the default report's level line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] `sed -n '656,719p' recommend-level.sh` shows the parser block this change extends\n- [ ] `recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints 17\n- [ ] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0 before the first edit\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] Every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is Met\n- [ ] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0 after the last edit\n- [ ] The quiet run prints 1 line and the default run prints 17\n- [ ] `diff` of the default report against the pre-change baseline prints nothing\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle-script output branch.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument parser** (`while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]` with `case \"$1\"`): turns argv into globals, one case per flag.\n- **`output_text()`**: writes the human report and owns the `Recommended Level:` line.\n- **`output_json()`**: writes the machine document; unchanged by this feature.\n- **`show_help()`**: renders the option list the flag must join.\n\n### Data Flow\nargv reaches the parser, which sets `LOC`, `FILES`, the four risk booleans, `JSON_OUTPUT` and the new `QUIET`. The score helpers turn those into `TOTAL_SCORE`, then `determine_level` sets `RECOMMENDED_LEVEL` and `LEVEL_NAME`. The output dispatch at the end of the script chooses `output_json` when `JSON_OUTPUT` is true, otherwise `output_text`, which prints the level line alone when `QUIET` is true and the full report otherwise.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n## FIX ADDENDUM: AFFECTED SURFACES\n\n| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |\n|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|\n| `recommend-level.sh` | Producer: owns the level line and the whole report | update | `grep -n 'Recommended Level' recommend-level.sh` prints one line |\n| Callers in skill workflows and docs | Consumers of stdout text; none parses the report programmatically | unchanged | `grep -rn 'recommend-level' .skilled/skills --include='*.sh'` returns the script itself only |\n| `--json` consumers | Read the JSON document, which `--quiet` never touches | not a consumer | `--json` output diffed before and after the change |\n| Script tests | No test file covers this script today | not a consumer | `ls runtime/cli/tests` lists no filename containing `recommend` |\n\nRequired inventories:\n- Same-class producers: `grep -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` prints one line, so the label has a single producer.\n- Consumers of changed symbols: `grep -rn 'recommend-level' .skilled/skills --include='*.sh'` finds no second script that calls it.\n- Matrix axes: output mode (text, quiet, json) × input validity (valid, missing required inputs, unknown option, conflicting mode).\n- Algorithm invariant: not applicable — this change adds no path, parser, redaction or resolver logic.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:affected-surfaces -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\n| Test Type | Scope | Tools |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| Unit | Parser acceptance for `--quiet`, the `--json` conflict and the unknown-option path | bash invocations, `$?`, stderr capture |\n| Integration | The text-output branch through `output_text()` | `wc -l` and `diff` against the pre-change baseline |\n| Regression | Default report and JSON document for the reference invocation | `diff` of pre-change and post-change output |\n| Manual | `--help` renders the new option in the same column format | `grep -c -- '--quiet'` on the help output |\n\nThe two assertions that decide the feature are a line count and a byte comparison: `--quiet` must print `1` line, and that line must equal the default report's `Recommended Level:` line byte for byte.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Dependency | Type | Status | Impact if Blocked |\n|------------|------|--------|-------------------|\n| bash 3.2+ | Internal | Green | The script cannot run; every verification step stops |\n| coreutils (`wc`, `diff`, `grep`) | Internal | Green | Verification assertions cannot be expressed; implementation still possible |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\n- **Trigger**: The default report changes, the level line moves, or the quiet run prints anything other than one line.\n- **Procedure**: Revert the single commit that touches `recommend-level.sh`. The flag is additive and the script holds no state, so no data or configuration needs unwinding.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n## L2: PHASE DEPENDENCIES\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Setup) ──► Phase 2 (Implementation) ──► Phase 3 (Verification)\n```\n\n| Phase | Depends On | Blocks |\n|-------|------------|--------|\n| Setup | None | Implementation |\n| Implementation | Setup | Verification |\n| Verification | Implementation | None |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-deps -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:effort -->\n## L2: EFFORT ESTIMATION\n\n| Phase | Complexity | Estimated Effort |\n|-------|------------|------------------|\n| Setup | Low | 10 minutes |\n| Core Implementation | Low | 20 minutes |\n| Verification | Low | 15 minutes |\n| **Total** | | **45 minutes (assumption)** |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:effort -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n## L2: ENHANCED ROLLBACK\n\n### Pre-deployment Checklist\n- [ ] Backup created (if data changes) — no data changes, so none needed\n- [ ] Feature flag configured — not applicable; the new flag is opt-in by invocation\n- [ ] Monitoring alerts set — not applicable; no service is deployed\n\n### Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert the commit that modifies `recommend-level.sh`.\n2. Run `bash -n` on the restored file.\n3. Re-run the reference invocation and confirm 17 lines and exit 0.\n4. Notify callers only if the flag had already been announced.\n\n### Data Reversal\n- **Has data migrations?** No\n- **Reversal procedure**: N/A — the script writes no file and holds no state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:enhanced-rollback -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n## L3: DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────┐\n│   Phase 1   │────►│   Phase 2   │────►│   Phase 3   │\n│   Setup     │     │    Core     │     │   Verify    │\n└─────────────┘     └─────────────┘     └─────────────┘\n```\n\n### Dependency Matrix\n\n| Component | Depends On | Produces | Blocks |\n|-----------|------------|----------|--------|\n| Baseline capture | None | Pre-change report and JSON fixtures | Implementation, Verification |\n| Parser and output branch | Baseline capture | One-line quiet mode | Verification |\n| Verification | Parser and output branch | Line-count and byte-equality evidence | Close |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependency-graph -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n## L3: CRITICAL PATH\n\n1. **Capture the pre-change baseline** - 10 minutes - CRITICAL\n2. **Add the parser case, conflict check and output branch** - 20 minutes - CRITICAL\n3. **Run the line-count and byte-equality checks** - 15 minutes - CRITICAL\n\n**Total Critical Path**: 45 minutes\n\n**Parallel Opportunities**:\n- Header and help text edits can land alongside the parser case once the wording is fixed.\n- The JSON regression check can run while the text-mode checks run, because neither writes a file.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:critical-path -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:milestones -->\n## L3: MILESTONES\n\n| Milestone | Description | Success Criteria | Target |\n|-----------|-------------|------------------|--------|\n| M1 | Baseline captured | `recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | wc -l` prints 17 | Phase 1 |\n| M2 | Quiet mode works | `... --quiet | wc -l` prints 1 and `diff` of the level lines is empty | Phase 2 |\n| M3 | Nothing else moved | Default report and JSON document diff clean against the baseline, `bash -n` exits 0 | Phase 3 |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:milestones -->\n\n---\n\n## L3: ARCHITECTURE DECISION RECORD\n\n### ADR-001: Gate the level line inside `output_text` instead of adding a second output function\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: The script has one text renderer, `output_text()`, which writes 17 lines including the level line. Quiet mode needs one of those lines and none of the others.\n\n**Decision**: Add a `QUIET` global set by the parser, then branch inside `output_text()` so it prints the level line and returns before the score, breakdown and phase blocks. Both modes read the same `echo`, so the line has one definition.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- The quiet line cannot drift from the report's level line, because both come from the same statement.\n- The function gains one early branch, and the phase block still computes in quiet mode; that arithmetic is wasted and is accepted so output and computation stay separate concerns.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- A separate `output_quiet()` function: duplicates the label string, so the two copies can drift.\n- Having callers pipe the report through `grep`: costs a second process, hides the script's own answer, and breaks on a label change just the same.\n\n### ADR-002: Reject `--quiet --json` with exit 1 instead of letting one flag win\n\n**Status**: Proposed\n\n**Context**: `--json` already emits a single machine document, and `--quiet` emits a single text line. A caller that passes both has asked for two different outputs.\n\n**Decision**: The parser records both booleans, and a check immediately after the parse loop writes an error naming both flags to stderr and exits 1.\n\n**Consequences**:\n- A contradictory invocation fails loudly instead of returning a shape the caller did not ask for.\n- Callers must choose one mode, and the help text states the exclusion so the failure is predictable.\n\n**Alternatives Rejected**:\n- JSON wins silently: the caller receives a document while believing it asked for a line, so the mistake surfaces far from its cause.\n- Quiet wins: a JSON consumer that adds the flag loses its document without a diagnostic.\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":1}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e